# Rust
/src-tauri/target/
**/*.rs.bk

# Generated by tauri-build on every compile, from tauri.conf.json and the
# capabilities files. Committing it means every build produces a spurious diff.
/src-tauri/gen/

# Node
node_modules/
dist/
.vite/

# Editors / OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp

# Local agent state
.claude/settings.local.json

# Build artifacts.
#
# `*.exe` is why an installer is not committed, and the rule is deliberate: a
# 3.2 MB binary that changes on every build cannot be delta-compressed, so every
# copy stays in the history at full size forever. One afternoon of iteration in
# this repository would have added ~40 MB that no `git rm` can take back out.
# The installers are published by CI — as a run artifact on every branch, and as
# a release asset on a tag — which is where a build belongs. `gh run download
# <run-id> -n marklet-setup` fetches one; nothing here needs to hold it.
*.exe
*.AppImage
*.deb
SHA256SUMS

# Test scratch
/tests/vault-synthetic/

# Generated exports of demo/demo.md
demo/*.html
demo/*.pdf
